config HMA_UIDFAKE
	bool "HMA uidfake built-in (kernel-side UID existence guard)"
	default n
	help
	  Built-in version of the hma-uidfake hook (getpriority/ioprio and the
	  task_fix_setuid tagging). Policy is fed from userspace over a generic
	  netlink family; with no policy loaded it is a pass-through no-op.
	  Equivalent to loading the hma_uidfake.ko module, but compiled in so it
	  needs no module artifact or ABI/profile matching.
